{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1785993593300939001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"idle-kiln-knelt","assignee":"Joe Oakhart","attestations":{"plan-review":{"algorithm":"HMAC-SHA256","author":"Iso Tester","head_sha":"c0e29406a3c7afa36268d8210036909e3642d2cd","key_id":"412fa5372ad877e0","kind":"plan-review","manifest":["plan-review: PASS","ticket: 4cb9-d88b-d891-42ad","material: 3aa3183d19fa1dd1","model: claude-sonnet-4-6","runner: pydantic_ai","blocking: 0","advisory: 2","regver: 83e5f63ad06d893a","dep 9dc7359bd6777a3bbb497e5a05151cbc358bda70031a880950f505d2c425367f docs/adr/0007-convergent-plan-edit-re-review.md","dep 3d58ea1f2739f24da25a2432b2a3b676164c8a002517ab579d20e6885f7742fd docs/plan-review-gate.md","dep 38b8f1ed5215e4a53bdcbce867405785fa776b2f0ff62341e1d85fdc936dad87 tests/unit/test_plan_review_convergence.py"],"signature":"c83f61d844989f63626e66a74391777c7bc0e9a3c8e8fa3171f5e24dfaa483e4","signed_at":1782787225766484000}},"author":"Iso Tester","authorship":{"signed":0,"unsigned":10},"authorship_ledger":[],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1782753997363534001,"creation_channel":"unknown","deps":[{"link_uuid":"05167bfb-a52d-40d5-af9b-9225f2735358","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"cc5b-cc69-79e1-4f27"},{"link_uuid":"e56f93d3-40d4-4568-aa93-d1222bd8384e","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"ec89-224e-1ca5-47f8"}],"description":"Document the remediation re-review and prove it offline. Add a `docs/plan-review-gate.md`\nsection AND an ADR under `docs/adr/` (recording the chosen design, the three rejected\nalternatives, and the invariants: Pass-1 unanchored; novelty in a SEPARATE Pass-2 sub-call;\ndrop decision deterministic in Pass-3). Add FakeRunner tests covering convergence on a\nremediation edit (novel low-priority dropped, carryover enforced, novel high-priority\npreserved) plus every precondition fallback to a byte-identical full review (code drift,\nwindow expiry, registry skew, no/old sidecar, config off).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `docs/plan-review-gate.md` section on the rising-floor remediation re-review\n- [ ] An ADR under `docs/adr/` records the design, 3 rejected alternatives, and the invariants\n- [ ] FakeRunner test: convergence on a remediation edit in `tests/unit/`\n- [ ] FakeRunner tests: each precondition fallback -> byte-identical full review\n- [ ] Test: novel high-priority preserved; carryover still enforced at the normal bar\n\n## Prerequisites (already delivered on this work branch — this task only CONSUMES them)\n\nThis task is the documentation + offline proof for machinery delivered by its sibling children,\nall already implemented and closed on the epic's work branch (a plan review grounding against\n`origin/main` will not see them yet — review this ticket with `--source local`):\n\n- **e344** — `sidecar.latest_review_result` / finding-prose persistence (the prior findings the\n  novelty sub-call re-grounds on).\n- **150b** — `decide.NOVELTY_SUBANSWERS` + `decide.novelty` (the deterministic novelty score),\n  `verify.score_novelty` + the registered `novelty` contract (the SEPARATE Pass-2 sub-call), and\n  the `discriminates_novelty` eval gate.\n- **ec89** — `attest.remediation_mode_candidate` (the freshness-window + precondition eligibility\n  decision) + the `verify.remediation_mode` / `remediation_window_minutes` config keys.\n- **cc5b** — `decide.rising_floor_drop` (the deterministic drop predicate) + the\n  `_apply_floor_to_verdict` / `_maybe_apply_rising_floor` seam in `_run_plan_review` + the\n  `verify.novelty_drop_threshold` / `novelty_priority_floor` / `novelty_drop_active` keys.\n\nThis task introduces NO new production mechanism — it adds the docs/ADR and FakeRunner tests that\nhook into these existing seams (the convergence test drives `score_novelty` via a\n`FakeRunner(structured={\"novelties\": ...})`; the precondition-fallback tests drive\n`remediation_mode_candidate` / `_maybe_apply_rising_floor` directly).","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"docs/plan-review-gate.md","reason":"section on the rising-floor remediation re-review"},{"path":"docs/adr/0007-convergent-plan-edit-re-review.md","reason":"ADR: design, 3 rejected alternatives, invariants"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_plan_review_convergence.py","reason":"FakeRunner convergence + precondition-fallback tests"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["depends_on","cc5b-cc69-79e1-4f27"],["depends_on","ec89-224e-1ca5-47f8"],["parent","7d43-49c5-bc4d-4926"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"7d43-49c5-bc4d-4926","parent_status_uuid":"aa9886bb-5775-44d4-9f0f-86b1d5fdab36","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"4cb9-d88b-d891-42ad","ticket_type":"task","title":"Docs + offline convergence tests for remediation re-review","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["e55ed974-2620-43bd-9476-6a99ba2dd76d","05167bfb-a52d-40d5-af9b-9225f2735358","e56f93d3-40d4-4568-aa93-d1222bd8384e","e2a2d67b-33c9-469d-8d4c-78e0ae240a1b","a8f2039c-ecc4-47d1-a455-c9ca21664e37","70265e6a-67aa-48dc-9eae-40f7115bbc50","b4716259-4c07-4ed6-933f-0645c11fe7d2","f6158a76-3746-4022-af9e-c9dfdd3fe712","38798bb9-2667-405e-b60b-e35ed3abd874","aa9886bb-5775-44d4-9f0f-86b1d5fdab36","6f374e14-5948-46d6-afa7-3f4a040eadaf","0e6ad35e-8bae-4714-8400-63f9e6778322"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785993593300939001,"uuid":"0a357a7e-3da5-438f-a53e-a506461c0980"}